$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6-Bromo-1-(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)pyridin-2(1H)-one (3). A mixture of
6-bromopyridin-2(1H)-one (2) (8.3 g, 47.7 mmol),
(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)boronic acid (20.1 g, 94.8 mmol), Cu(OAc)2 (0.9
g, 5.0 mmol), pyridine (7.7 mL, 94.8 mmol), pyridine-N-oxide (5.0 g, 52.6
mmol), 4Å MS (2.0 g) and dry CH2Cl2 (100 mL) was stirred under dry air at
room temperature overnight. Then added CH2Cl2 (300 mL) and NH3·H2O (25%,
50 mL), and the reaction mixture was filtered through Celite, washed with
CH2Cl2. The filtrate was washed with water, dried over Na2SO4. The
solvent was evaporated to dryness to yield the crude product, which was
triturated with CH2Cl2 (50 mL). a white solid (13.0 g, 77% yield). Mp:
174.9-176.8 °C ; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.51 (t, J=7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.20
(d, J=7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.74 (d, J=8.1 Hz, 1H), 6.40 (s, 2H), 3.84 (s, 3H),
3.82 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.12, 153.79, 149.69, 141.25,
139.32, 135.28, 122.44, 109.15, 98.56, 98.50, 61.00, 56.18.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM molecular sieves used, Chan-Lam coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and in vitro cytotoxic evaluation of novel
N-(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)pyridin-2(1H)-one derivatives
